// The deployment these apps are built for: the host their release builds
// talk to and whose links open in them. Copy this file to deployment.local
// (which is not committed) and put your deployment's host there; a build
// with neither file, or with this one alone, is for meet.example.com and
// reaches nothing. Read by the core's build (core/protocol/build.rs), the
// Apple targets (apple/Deployment.xcconfig) and Android's Gradle build; the
// environment's TOMOSHIBI_HOST, where set, is taken before either file.
TOMOSHIBI_HOST = meet.example.com

// The public half of the deployment's release key, as 64 hexadecimal digits:
// the Ed25519 key, kept on no server, that signs each build's line of the
// deployment's apps.json (its "sig"). The core holds every update to it
// before a build is offered or downloaded (core/protocol/src/api/updates.rs),
// so a deployment's server, or the folder its builds are shelved in, cannot
// hand the apps a build of its own. A release build for a real deployment
// does not build without one. The example deployment has none, and a build
// for it takes a key from the environment alone. A debug build pointed at a
// local deployment whose manifest nobody signed may say "none". Used by the
// core's build alone; the environment's TOMOSHIBI_UPDATE_KEY, where set, is
// taken before either file.
// TOMOSHIBI_UPDATE_KEY = <64 hexadecimal digits>
